title: ActTwoNotes
act: Wreck
style: note
---
Act II, one day. A ship came in the night\: at anchor if the lamp burned, on the rocks if not. The town meets at the bell (a hub that detours into each topic). The courier takes a side on the cargo, follows three signs of Odile, and may win the trust of the stranger. #line:0c4256b
===

title: ActTwo
act: Wreck
scenario: Salvage
quest: salvage
---
// The night events of Act I jump here
<<set $act = Act.Wreck>>
<<set $wren_here = true>>
<<end_day>>
<<if $wreck_aground>>
    Morning. The ship lies broken on the north rocks, and her crates ride the surf. Her crew is safe at the inn, and one passenger with them. #line:0d6e514
<<else>>
    Morning. The ship rides at anchor in the bay. The boats brought her cargo ashore before the gale, and one passenger with it. #line:0f30fff
<<endif>>
The bell by the harbour office is ringing\: a town meeting. #line:06bdbaa
<<set $quest_salvage = QuestState.Active>>
<<quest_changed salvage>>
===

title: Bell
act: Wreck
scenario: Salvage
when: $act == Act.Wreck
---
<<jump TownMeeting>>
===

title: TownMeeting
act: Wreck
scenario: Salvage
cluster: Town meeting
color: green
---
<<if visited("TownMeeting")>>
    The meeting has not ended. It may never end. #line:03e94d7
<<else>>
    Half the island stands around the bell. Everyone is talking. Nobody is listening. #line:0cbbd01
<<endif>>
<<jump MeetingTopics>>
===

title: MeetingTopics
act: Wreck
scenario: Salvage
cluster: Town meeting
color: green
---
// The hub of the meeting: each topic is a detour that comes back here
-> Ask about the cargo. <<if $side == Side.Neither>> #line:06ca130
    <<detour MeetingCargo>>
    <<jump MeetingTopics>>
-> Ask about the keeper. <<if not visited("MeetingKeeper")>> #line:023f405
    <<detour MeetingKeeper>>
    <<jump MeetingTopics>>
-> Ask about the stranger. <<if not visited("MeetingStranger")>> #line:0380bca
    <<detour MeetingStranger>>
    <<jump MeetingTopics>>
-> Leave them to it. #line:0b3eb43
===

title: MeetingCargo
act: Wreck
scenario: Salvage
quest: salvage
cluster: Town meeting
color: green
---
<<if $wreck_aground>>
    Maud: Wreck goods belong to whoever pulls them from the sea. That is the custom, and we pulled. #line:028a3b1
    Brandt: The debts are older than the custom. The harbour takes the cargo. #line:02345af
<<else>>
    Maud: We rowed that cargo ashore in a gale. We are owed for it. #line:08cd5fb
    Brandt: Her captain owes the harbour first. The cargo stays under my lock. #line:0c29c0b
<<endif>>
Maud: Ask the post. The post has no boat and no desk. #line:051c593
-> The boats should have it. #line:0c2b616
    <<set $side = Side.Fishers>>
    Maud: There. Thank you, courier. #mood:glad #line:0c2c6d9
    Brandt: The post should carry letters. #mood:angry #line:09c623d
-> The harbour should hold it. #line:0b45ecd
    <<set $side = Side.Harbour>>
    Brandt: Sense, at last. #line:03ce77a
    Maud: I thought better of you. #mood:angry #line:03b69fc
-> I carry letters. I take no side. #line:01fea03
    Maud: Then come back when you have one. #line:0f5801f
<<if $side != Side.Neither>>
    <<set $quest_salvage = QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed salvage>>
<<endif>>
===

title: MeetingKeeper
act: Wreck
scenario: Odile's trail
quest: trail
cluster: Town meeting
color: green
---
Tam: Four days now. Odile does not just leave. #mood:afraid #line:0e316ea
Joss: Somebody saw her walk north along the shore, the night before the lamp went dark. #line:0397f86
Tam: You walk everywhere, courier. Look for her. Look for anything of hers. #line:0ca764a
<<if $quest_trail == QuestState.NotStarted>>
    <<set $quest_trail = QuestState.Active>>
    <<quest_changed trail>>
<<endif>>
===

title: MeetingStranger
act: Wreck
scenario: The stranger
cluster: Town meeting
color: green
---
Joss: The passenger? Wren, she calls herself. Came off that ship with one bag and no reason. #line:00a7ae2
Tam: She is outside the Anchor. She has not eaten, and she watches the lighthouse. #line:0f6e0a6
===

title: Brandt
act: Wreck
scenario: Salvage
quest: salvage
when: $act == Act.Wreck and $side == Side.Neither
---
Brandt: That cargo pays the harbour's debts. Say so at the bell, courier, and I will remember it. #line:02d0a03
===

title: Maud
act: Wreck
scenario: Salvage
quest: salvage
when: $act == Act.Wreck and $side == Side.Neither
---
Maud: Brandt wants the cargo for his ledgers. Speak for the boats at the bell. #line:0e92fd0
===

title: Boot
act: Wreck
scenario: Odile's trail
quest: trail
when: $act == Act.Wreck and not $clue_boot
---
A sea boot, wedged in the rocks above the tide line. There is lamp soot on the leather\: a keeper's boot. #line:0c03b93
<<set $clue_boot = true>>
<<detour ClueFound>>
===

title: Lantern
act: Wreck
scenario: Odile's trail
quest: trail
when: $act == Act.Wreck and not $clue_lantern
---
A signal lantern with green glass, hidden under the north rocks. Someone has been calling boats in, where there is no harbour. #line:0a32297
<<set $clue_lantern = true>>
<<detour ClueFound>>
===

title: LighthouseDoor
act: Wreck
scenario: Odile's trail
quest: trail
when: $act == Act.Wreck and not $clue_ledger
---
The door stands open. Somebody searched the place in the night. #line:05a61cb
On the stair, pages torn from a ledger, in Odile's hand. Dates, and beside each one\: "lamp out, by order. B." #line:05a5fa3
<<give pages>>
<<set $clue_ledger = true>>
<<detour ClueFound>>
===

title: ClueFound
act: Wreck
scenario: Odile's trail
quest: trail
---
// Said after each sign is found
<<set $clues_found = $clues_found + 1>>
<<if $quest_trail == QuestState.NotStarted>>
    <<set $quest_trail = QuestState.Active>>
    <<quest_changed trail>>
<<endif>>
That is the [ordinal value={$clues_found} one="%st" two="%nd" few="%rd" other="%th" /] sign of Odile. #line:048d074
===

title: Events
act: Wreck
scenario: Odile's trail
quest: trail
when: $act == Act.Wreck
when: $trail_complete and $quest_trail == QuestState.Active
---
A boot, a ledger, a green lantern. They point the same way\: the cave under the north rocks. #line:0128805
The ledge to the cave is under water until tomorrow. #line:04d5bda
<<set $quest_trail = QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed trail>>
===

title: Wren
act: Wreck
scenario: The stranger
when: $act == Act.Wreck and not $wren_met
---
<<set $wren_met = true>>
<<if $wreck_aground>>
    Wren: You are the post. I was on that ship when she struck. I would like to know why. #line:05082f1
<<else>>
    Wren: You are the post. I watched your lamp from the deck last night. It came on late. #line:0b3f112
<<endif>>
Wren: Who lit the lamp last night? Or who did not? #line:0eea3ce
-> I lit it myself. The keeper is missing. <<if $lamp_lit>> #line:0abd2da
    <<set $wren_trust = $wren_trust + 1>>
    Wren: The post lights the lamp. Then somebody here is honest. #line:0731753
-> Nobody did. I was too late. <<if not $lamp_lit>> #line:06c9ae0
    <<set $wren_trust = $wren_trust + 1>>
    Wren: That is not an easy thing to say. Thank you for saying it. #line:0acaf3d
-> Ask the harbourmaster. #line:04da9d1
    Wren: I will. I wanted to ask someone else first. #line:0340960
===

title: Wren
act: All
scenario: The stranger
quest: meal
when: $quest_meal == QuestState.Active and has_item("stew")
---
<<take stew>>
Wren: From the innkeeper? [pause=500 /]He asks a great many questions. You only brought stew. #line:0020874
<<set $wren_trust = $wren_trust + 1>>
<<set $quest_meal = QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed meal>>
===

title: Wren
act: All
when: always
---
<<if $wren_stands>>
    Wren: I will ring for myself. It feels strange. #line:01f880d
<<else>>
    => Wren: I am watching the lighthouse. It is my work, in a way. #line:05a1a71
    => Wren: It is a small island. Everyone knows everything, and nobody says it. #line:0fe3500
<<endif>>
===

title: Tam
act: Wreck
scenario: The stranger
quest: meal
when: $act == Act.Wreck and $quest_meal == QuestState.NotStarted
---
Tam: That passenger has not eaten since she came ashore. She will not take a bowl from me. #line:07d8112
Tam: I asked where she was from. And why. And for how long. #mood:sad #line:08c8bfb
-> Give me the bowl. I will take it to her. #line:077ed21
    <<give stew>>
    <<set $quest_meal = QuestState.Active>>
    <<quest_changed meal>>
    Tam: Tell her it is fish. It is nearly fish. #line:08969ad
-> She will eat when she is hungry. #line:03620cb
    Tam: That is what I am afraid of. #line:03aea79
===

title: Events
act: Wreck
when: $act == Act.Wreck
when: $is_night
---
<<if $quest_trail == QuestState.Active>>
    Night. The trail of Odile goes cold in the dark. #line:00c1198
    <<set $quest_trail = QuestState.Failed>>
    <<quest_changed trail>>
<<endif>>
<<if $quest_salvage == QuestState.Active>>
    While the town sleeps, Brandt has the cargo carried to the harbour store. #line:017333a
    <<set $quest_salvage = QuestState.Failed>>
    <<quest_changed salvage>>
<<endif>>
<<jump ActThree>>
===
